            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Why defense ETFs and gold miner ETFs are seeing big inflows",
            "description": "<p>Defense stocks have cooled off since their <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/oil-prices-defense-stocks-jump-133040000.html\">recent surge</a>, but defense-related exchange-traded funds (ETFs) are still seeing inflows as NATO leaders commit 5% of their annual budgets to defense spending.</p>\n<p>Cinthia Murphy, VettaFi investment strategist, joins Market Catalysts to explain how these flows signal defense as both a tech and industrial play. She also takes a look at gold miner ETFs and explains why they're among the market's top performers this year.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more Market Catalysts\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">here</a>.</p>",
